CodeRabbit/Codex re-reviewed 4e21b53c and opened 4 new threads — all valid
consequences of the prior fixes:

- orientation.js (P2 + data-integrity): the read-only gate wrongly suppressed
  live state for BEADS-backend projects (they have no kernel.sqlite by design).
  Now backend-aware via shouldSkipLiveSnapshot: require an existing Kernel DB ONLY
  on the kernel path; Beads reads .beads via bd (non-creating) and is not gated.
- agents-config.js (P2): the generated AGENTS.md dispatch pointer named a
  repo-relative skills/using-forge/SKILL.md, which does not exist in a set-up
  consumer project (only the generated mirrors do). Now references the skill BY
  NAME (auto-discovered from the agent's own skills dir) + `forge skill for`.
- skill.js (SonarCloud S1788): removed the non-final default param — dropped the
  unused trailing `_projectRoot` so `flags = {}` is the last declared param.

Tests: backend-aware gate unit test (kernel-no-DB skipped, beads not); parity test
asserts the pointer names the skill by name, not a repo path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
